WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:23.072
The Umbrella by Clare Harris.

00:00:23.132 --> 00:00:27.104
It is raining.

00:00:27.164 --> 00:00:29.816
The sky is grey.

00:00:29.876 --> 00:00:33.277
Carla goes to the market.

00:00:33.338 --> 00:00:36.018
She looks at the umbrellas.

00:00:36.078 --> 00:00:38.944
She likes a red umbrella.

00:00:39.003 --> 00:00:41.298
It's very smart.

00:00:41.358 --> 00:00:44.420
It costs ten dollars.

00:00:44.479 --> 00:00:47.381
Carla is a student.

00:00:47.442 --> 00:00:50.603
She doesn't have much money.

00:00:50.663 --> 00:00:55.246
I can give you seven dollars for that umbrella.

00:00:55.306 --> 00:00:57.346
OK, young lady.

00:00:57.406 --> 00:00:59.998
This is your lucky day.

00:01:00.058 --> 00:01:02.279
Give me seven dollars.

00:01:02.339 --> 00:01:05.771
The umbrella is yours.

00:01:05.831 --> 00:01:09.395
This is my lucky day!

00:01:09.455 --> 00:01:11.288
says Carla.

00:01:11.348 --> 00:01:15.500
She holds the red umbrella above her head.

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:19.472
The rain falls on the umbrella.

00:01:19.532 --> 00:01:23.234
Carla goes to a cake shop.

00:01:23.294 --> 00:01:26.176
She wants to buy some cakes.

00:01:26.236 --> 00:01:29.908
Her little brother loves cakes.

00:01:29.968 --> 00:01:32.630
She goes into the shop.

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:37.157
She leaves her red umbrella near the door.

00:01:37.216 --> 00:01:41.212
It is quiet inside the shop.

00:01:41.272 --> 00:01:45.206
Carla chooses three small cakes.

00:01:45.266 --> 00:01:48.617
She talks to the shop assistant.

00:01:48.678 --> 00:01:52.280
A customer is leaving the shop.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:54.872
She is a young woman.

00:01:54.932 --> 00:01:58.654
She is holding a cake box.

00:01:58.714 --> 00:02:02.607
Carla is going to leave the shop.

00:02:02.666 --> 00:02:06.363
But where is her umbrella?

00:02:06.423 --> 00:02:10.160
There is one umbrella near the door.

00:02:10.219 --> 00:02:13.691
It is not a red umbrella.

00:02:13.751 --> 00:02:17.513
It is not Carla's umbrella.

00:02:17.573 --> 00:02:22.025
This umbrella is old and black.

00:02:22.085 --> 00:02:25.546
It has a pattern of yellow ducks.

00:02:25.606 --> 00:02:27.958
It is not smart.

00:02:28.018 --> 00:02:32.100
Carla takes the umbrella.

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:37.266
This is not my lucky day!

00:02:37.326 --> 00:02:41.064
Carla walks to the town square.

00:02:41.124 --> 00:02:44.316
A young man speaks to her.

00:02:44.376 --> 00:02:48.628
Hello! He smiles.
 
00:02:48.688 --> 00:02:52.230
Carla does not know this young man.

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:55.563
She walks away quickly.

00:02:55.623 --> 00:02:59.846
The young man is following Carla.

00:02:59.906 --> 00:03:03.359
She walks into a crowd of people.

00:03:03.418 --> 00:03:08.300
The young man follows the black and yellow umbrella.

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:11.822
Hello! Wait!
 
00:03:11.882 --> 00:03:14.462
Carla turns.

00:03:14.522 --> 00:03:17.374
She looks at the young man.

00:03:17.434 --> 00:03:19.456
She is angry.

00:03:19.516 --> 00:03:22.847
Go away! she says.
 
00:03:22.907 --> 00:03:25.738
The young man is sad.

00:03:25.798 --> 00:03:28.270
Marisa, I'm sorry!

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:31.842
he says. I'm very late.

00:03:31.902 --> 00:03:36.214
I'm not Marisa! Carla shouts.
 
00:03:36.274 --> 00:03:40.773
You are not Marisa? says the young man.
 
00:03:40.833 --> 00:03:45.364
He points at the black umbrella with yellow ducks.

00:03:45.424 --> 00:03:47.904
That's her umbrella.

00:03:47.964 --> 00:03:51.255
Oh, says Carla.
 
00:03:51.315 --> 00:03:54.056
Who is Marisa?

00:03:54.116 --> 00:03:58.866
I don't know Marisa, says the young man.
 
00:03:58.926 --> 00:04:01.427
I'm going to meet her.

00:04:01.487 --> 00:04:04.728
We are going to have coffee.

00:04:04.788 --> 00:04:08.140
It is my cousin's idea.

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:11.733
Marisa works with my cousin.

00:04:11.792 --> 00:04:16.844
I am not Marisa! says Carla again.
 
00:04:16.904 --> 00:04:20.684
My cousin has a photo of Marisa,

00:04:20.744 --> 00:04:22.554
says the young man.

00:04:22.614 --> 00:04:26.355
She's tall. You're tall.
 
00:04:26.415 --> 00:04:30.026
Her hair is short and dark.

00:04:30.086 --> 00:04:33.496
Your hair is short and dark.

00:04:33.556 --> 00:04:37.488
In the photo, she has an umbrella.

00:04:37.548 --> 00:04:42.213
It's a black umbrella with yellow ducks.

00:04:42.272 --> 00:04:48.537
You have a black umbrella with yellow ducks!

00:04:48.597 --> 00:04:53.881
Carla looks up at the old umbrella.

00:04:53.941 --> 00:04:57.614
Marisa is a thief, she thinks.
 
00:04:57.674 --> 00:05:00.956
She has my new red umbrella.

00:05:01.016 --> 00:05:04.449
Carla is angry again.

00:05:04.509 --> 00:05:09.938
Please don't be angry, says the young man.
  
00:05:09.998 --> 00:05:12.638
He looks at his watch.

00:05:12.698 --> 00:05:15.169
It's three o'clock.

00:05:15.229 --> 00:05:19.430
Marisa goes to work at two thirty.

00:05:19.490 --> 00:05:22.120
I can't meet her now.

00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:24.561
It's too late.

00:05:24.621 --> 00:05:27.732
He smiles at Carla.

00:05:27.792 --> 00:05:32.273
Let's have coffee together, he says.

00:05:32.333 --> 00:05:36.000
Carla thinks for a moment.

00:05:36.059 --> 00:05:38.617
OK, she says.
 
00:05:38.676 --> 00:05:41.679
Let's go to my aunt's cafe.

00:05:41.738 --> 00:05:44.802
The young man smiles again.

00:05:44.862 --> 00:05:49.004
That will be great, he says.

00:05:49.064 --> 00:05:52.197
My name is Paul.

00:05:52.257 --> 00:05:56.470
I'm a law student. Third year.
 
00:05:56.530 --> 00:06:00.634
I'm Carla. I'm a student too.
 
00:06:00.694 --> 00:06:04.143
I'm studying science.

00:06:04.202 --> 00:06:09.590
Carla sits in the cafe with Paul.

00:06:09.650 --> 00:06:12.351
They drink coffee.

00:06:12.411 --> 00:06:19.992
They talk. They laugh. They laugh and talk.
 
00:06:20.052 --> 00:06:24.263
Suddenly, Carla jumps up.

00:06:24.323 --> 00:06:27.034
Oh, no! she says.
 
00:06:27.094 --> 00:06:28.504
It's late.

00:06:28.564 --> 00:06:30.254
I must go home.

00:06:30.314 --> 00:06:32.150
I must study.

00:06:32.210 --> 00:06:35.478
I'm going to have an exam tomorrow.

00:06:35.537 --> 00:06:37.660
Good luck!

00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:40.312
Will you meet me again?

00:06:40.372 --> 00:06:44.933
Yes. That will be nice.
 
00:06:44.993 --> 00:06:48.694
It is almost dark.

00:06:48.754 --> 00:06:52.516
The town square is quiet.

00:06:52.576 --> 00:06:57.177
Carla sees a tall young woman.

00:06:57.237 --> 00:07:02.429
The young woman has short dark hair.

00:07:02.489 --> 00:07:06.306
She has a smart umbrella.

00:07:06.366 --> 00:07:09.523
It is a red umbrella.

00:07:09.582 --> 00:07:14.306
The young woman is Marisa!

00:07:14.366 --> 00:07:20.770
Marisa sees the old black umbrella with yellow ducks.

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:23.292
She is worried.

00:07:23.352 --> 00:07:27.136
Suddenly, her face is red.

00:07:27.196 --> 00:07:30.268
Don't worry, says Carla.

00:07:30.328 --> 00:07:32.730
Keep my red umbrella.

00:07:32.790 --> 00:07:35.154
I like this umbrella.

00:07:35.213 --> 00:07:37.298
It's a lucky umbrella.

00:07:37.358 --> 00:07:40.523
This is my lucky day!

00:07:40.583 --> 00:07:44.138
The rain falls on the umbrellas.

00:07:44.198 --> 00:07:46.741
Carla smiles.

00:07:46.801 --> 00:08:04.000
Then she runs home.